Even though Athens is a fairly small college town, it's had a huge and important music scene for decades and the most famous band to come out of the Athens scene. Undoubtedly, was R-E-M. To be provocative right from the start, I'm going to say that REM's out of time is the most politically important album in the history of the United States. And this provocateur is reporter Whitney Jones, though I have to say, I don't think out of time is even the most important album in the history of REM. Actually my argument here has nothing to do with the music. This isn't one of those, oh it's a soundtrack to a generation or anything like that.
尽管雅典是一个相当小的大学城，但几十年来它一直拥有庞大且重要的音乐界，而从雅典走出来的最著名的乐队毫无疑问就是 R-E-M。为了从一开始就语出惊人，我要说的是，REM 的《Out of Time》是美国历史上政治上最重要的专辑。而这位语不惊人死不休的挑衅者是记者惠特尼·琼斯，不过我必须得说，我认为《Out of Time》甚至都不是 REM 历史上最重要的专辑。其实我这里的论点和音乐毫无关系。这可不是那种“哦，这是一代人的原声带”之类的说法。

3
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:35.000
Out of time made such a huge impact because of its packaging. The box that out of time originally came in led to a bill being passed in Congress and an actual concrete law. Let's go back to 1985. The pop charts were full of prints and Shina Easton and the youth of America were being corrupted. Tipper Gore and a few other elite women of Washington formed the Parents Music Resource Center, or the PMRC for short.
《Out of Time》之所以产生如此巨大的影响，是因为它的包装。当年《Out of Time》发售时使用的那个盒子，促使国会通过了一项法案并制定了一项切实的法律。让我们回到 1985 年。当时的流行音乐排行榜上到处都是普林斯（Prince）和希娜·伊斯顿（Sheena Easton），美国的年轻人正在被腐蚀。蒂珀·戈尔（Tipper Gore）和华盛顿的其他几位精英女性成立了“家长音乐资源中心”，简称 PMRC。

4
00:01:35.000 --> 00:02:24.000
They put pressure on the creators and distributors of quote unquote, objectionable music. Musicians and labels called this censorship. There were senate hearings about this, and eventually those little black and white parental advisory stickers started appearing on albums. This set off a wave of censorship across the country. In 1990, a federal district judge in South Florida ruled that the rap group Two Live Crews album, as nasty as they want to be, was so obscene that it couldn't be sold or performed within his jurisdiction. Three days after the ruling, two live crew played a show in Broward County, Florida, and after the show, two members of the group got arrested. And it was a live performance, I believe, that they found obscene with, you know, girls
他们对所谓“令人反感”的音乐的创作者和发行商施加压力。音乐人和唱片公司称这是审查制度。国会为此举行了听证会，最终，那些带有黑白字样的家长指引贴纸开始出现在专辑上。这在全国掀起了一股审查浪潮。1990 年，南佛罗里达州的一名联邦地区法官裁定，说唱组合“2 Live Crew”的专辑《As Nasty As They Want To Be》极其下流，以至于在他的司法管辖区内不得出售或演出。在这项裁决三天后，“2 Live Crew”在佛罗里达州布劳沃德县进行了一场演出，演出结束后，该组合的两名成员被捕。我相信正是那场现场演出被他们发现有伤风化，你知道的，女孩们

5
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:51.000
doing what would be like what my twerking, I think it that they found obscene with, you know, girls doing what would be like what my twerking, I think it would be a very early version of the twerking. Jeff Aerov wasn't there, he saw it on TV. And I just, it was just so offensive to me. Jeff was an executive at Virgin Records, and to be clear, he wasn't offended by the Ranchi lyrics or the twerking. He was offended by the arrests and the blatant censorship of the artist's work. Jeff spent the next couple of days mowing this over and then he had a revelation.
做着类似于我现在说的扭臀舞的动作，我认为这就是他们认为下流的地方，你知道的，女孩们做着类似于我现在说的扭臀舞的动作，我认为这可以说是早期版本的扭臀舞。杰夫·艾罗夫（Jeff Ayroff）当时不在现场，他在电视上看到的。我只是觉得，这对我来说太冒犯了。杰夫是维京唱片公司（Virgin Records）的高管，需要说明的是，他并没有被那些下流的歌词或扭臀舞所冒犯。真正冒犯他的是逮捕行动以及对艺术家作品的赤裸裸的审查。杰夫在接下来的几天里反复琢磨这件事，然后他有了一个顿悟。

6
00:02:51.000 --> 00:03:22.000
One of the reasons why politicians get away with things because there isn't an anti-constituency. There was never anything to lose by baiting rock and roll because there was this canard that young people didn't vote. And you know, within the next two days, the idea came to me like fully formed in some way and I came up with this name, Rock the Vote. For Jeff Aeroff, the idea behind Rock the Vote was simple. Get young people to vote for politicians who wouldn't censor music.
政客们之所以能逃脱惩罚，原因之一就是缺乏一个反向选民群体。利用摇滚乐来哗众取宠从来没什么好失去的，因为有一种谣言认为年轻人不投票。你知道的，在接下来的两天里，这个想法不知怎么的就完全成型了，我想出了这个名字——“摇滚选民”（Rock the Vote）。对杰夫·艾罗夫来说，“摇滚选民”背后的理念很简单：让年轻人投票给那些不会审查音乐的政客。

7
00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:43.000
Yeah, it was that simple. It was the idea if you put kids in the game. The game becomes different. Politicians can no longer scapegoat music. They can't keep using us as an excuse. So Jeff Aeroff got about 60 people together in a Los Angeles hotel to talk about launching Rock the Vote. For example, was there, past and present California governor, Jerry Brown,
是的，就是这么简单。这个想法就是，如果你把孩子们拉进这场游戏。游戏规则就变了。政客们不能再把音乐当作替罪羊。他们不能再拿我们当借口了。于是杰夫·艾罗夫把大约 60 个人召集到洛杉矶的一家酒店，讨论发起“摇滚选民”运动。例如，当时人在现场的、前任及现任加州州长杰里·布朗（Jerry Brown），

