Also named Jeff. Jeff Gold. He was working for Warner Brothers, and one of his major projects at the time was trying to figure out how to package CDs. Compact disc packaging was the hot topic in the record world in the late 80s and early 90s. CDs have been around for a few years at this point, but record stores still didn't have a good way to display them.
也叫杰夫。杰夫·戈尔（Jeff Gold）。他当时在华纳兄弟公司（Warner Brothers）工作，当时他的主要项目之一就是想方设法为 CD 设计包装。光盘包装是 80 年代末和 90 年代初唱片界的热门话题。当时 CD 已经问世几年了，但唱片店仍然没有一个展示它们的好方法。

10
00:04:30.000 --> 00:05:12.000
Here's Jeff Gold. When CDs first came out on the market, record retailers were kind of angry about them because their stores were formatted to display 12 and a inch or 12.4 inch squares albums. In other words, they didn't have any stands or display cases for these new CDs. So somebody in the record industry said, look, if you put a CD jewel case inside of a cardboard box that's as long as a vinyl album and only half is wide, you can fit two of these long box CDs side by side in an LP rack. Problem solved. And the Ricker retellers said fine, perfect. And so millions of these things
这位是杰夫·戈尔。当 CD 刚推向市场时，唱片零售商对它们有点生气，因为他们的店铺格局是专为展示 12.5 英寸或 12.4 英寸的正方形黑胶专辑而设计的。换句话说，他们没有任何适合这些新 CD 的展架或展示柜。于是唱片行业里的某个人说，听着，如果你把 CD 珠宝盒（CD jewel case）装在一个硬纸板盒里，这个盒子和黑胶专辑一样长，但宽度只有一半，你就可以在黑胶唱片架上并排放置两个这种长盒 CD。问题完美解决。唱片零售商说好，太棒了。于是数以百万计的这种东西

