out of nowhere started getting made. Record people loved the long box. They thought it was the future. A headhunt show at EMI wrote this opinion piece in Billboard magazine in 1989 entitled, Why We Should Keep The CD Longbox. He writes, quote, I want to see the music industry continue to thrive and prosper as one of the cornerstones of entertainment. And I think making full use of the 6x12 CD-Cardin is one way to help us do just that. But not everyone loved the long box. Artists said, wait a minute, we don't want you cutting down
凭空开始被制造出来。唱片界的人士非常喜欢长盒。他们认为这就是未来。EMI 的唱片高管肖恩（Headhunt show at EMI）于 1989 年在《公告牌》（Billboard）杂志上发表了一篇题为《为什么我们应该保留 CD 长盒》（Why We Should Keep The CD Longbox）的专栏文章。他写道：“我希望看到音乐产业继续蓬勃发展，成为娱乐业的基石之一。我认为充分利用 6x12 的 CD 卡纸是帮助我们做到这一点的途径之一。”但并不是所有人都喜欢这个长盒。艺术家们说，等一下，我们可不想让你们砍倒

