00:06:44.000 --> 00:07:16.000
They could use the CD Longbox to advance the Rock the Vote campaign. But first he needed a concrete political cause to connect it to. And Jeff Eroff had found just the thing. We were sitting there looking for a raison d'être to get us into a political situation. I'm reading Newsweek or Time and there's this column article about the Motor voter bill. We just said, we're going to help these people from the motor voter bill. This was going to be our first thing we were going to do. So there's this motor voter bill that's been bouncing around Congress since the 1970s.
他们可以利用 CD 长盒来推进“摇滚选民”运动。但首先，他需要一个具体的政治诉求来与之建立联系。而杰夫·艾罗夫刚好找到了这样的诉求。我们当时坐在那里寻找一个存在的理由（raison d'être），好让我们切入政治局势。我正在读《新闻周刊》（Newsweek）或《时代周刊》（Time），上面有一篇关于“机动选民法案”（Motor Voter Bill）的专栏文章。我们当时就说，我们要支持这些支持“机动选民法案”的人。这将是我们要做得第一件事。所以这个“机动选民法案”自 20 世纪 70 年代以来一直在国会里兜兜转转。

15
00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:55.000
If passed, motor voter would allow people to register to vote at the DMV when you got a driver's license. It also allowed you to register by mail or when you applied for social services like welfare or unemployment, basically making it easier for lots of people, including rock-loving young people, to register to vote. By 91, a few states had already adopted it, but Congress had never been able to get it passed nationally. Jeff Gold went to a political event in Hollywood about the motorboat or bill. And one of the speakers was Columbia sociologist and political activist Richard Cloud. He said that writing to elected officials could help sway them on the issue. After Cloud's talk, Jeff Gold went up and spoke with him.
如果通过，“机动选民”将允许人们在车管所（DMV）办驾照时登记投票。它还允许你通过邮政登记，或者在申请福利或失业救济等社会服务时进行登记，基本上让许多人（包括热爱摇滚的年轻人）更容易登记投票。到 91 年时，已经有一些州通过了该法案，但国会从未能在全国范围内使其通过。杰夫·戈尔去好莱坞参加了一个关于“机动选民法案”的政治活动。其中一位演讲者是哥伦比亚大学社会学家兼政治活动家理查德·克劳德（Richard Cloud）。他说，写信给民选官员可以帮助他们在议题上左右他们的看法。克劳德演讲结束后，杰夫·戈尔走过去跟他交谈。

