And went up and I started talking to him. And I said, what amount of letters would a Senator or a congressman take note of on a particular issue when he said, oh, 150, 200, that would really have any impact. And I said, really that few, he said, yeah, that, you know, people don't write. So getting 150, 200 letters about an issue would definitely make them sit up and take notice. That weekend, Jeff Gold was writing his bike around Santa Monica. And I had this moment where it rushed into my mind this fully formed idea that uh... we could
