members of the hip-hop group KMD, wheeled a shopping cart full of these first 10,000 petitions into a Senate hearing. And they just left them there for Senators' Windall Ford and a very young-looking Mitch McConnell. In May of 1992, after thousands of petitions and Senate testimony, the Motor Voter Bill passed Congress. But then President H.W. Bush vetoed it. This was in July right in the middle of Bush's re-election campaign. Bush's opponent, Bill Clinton,
嘻哈组合 KMD 的两名成员，推着一辆购物车，里面装满了前 10,000 份请愿书，走进了参议院听证会。他们把它们留给了参议员温德尔·福特（Wendall Ford）和看起来非常年轻的米奇·麦康奈尔（Mitch McConnell）。1992 年 5 月，在经历了数千份请愿书和参议院听证会之后，“机动选民法案”在国会获得通过。但当时的总统老布什（H.W. Bush）否决了它。那是 7 月份，正值老布什竞选连任的白热化阶段。布什的对手比尔·克林顿（Bill Clinton），

